@node TOOL "Tooltype Configuration"

                           @{bg fill}@{fg highlight} TOOLTYPE CONFIGURATION @{fg text}@{bg background}

 This door configures by tooltypes, (Doors:Request/Request.info):

 Template: BULL.OUTPUT=<path:filename>
 Example.: BULL.OUTPUT=BBS:Conf.Requests/Bull.txt
 Usage...: Destination path including textfile for creation of bulletin/list
           of requested files.

 Template: BULL.HEADER=<path:filename>
 Example.: BULL.HEADER=Doors:Request/Header.txt
 Usage...: Headertext to use in the bulletin created via "BULL.OUTPUT".

 Template: BULL.TAIL=<path:filename>
 Example.: BULL.TAIL=Doors:Request/Tailer.txt
 Usage...: Tailtext to use in the bulletin created via "BULL.OUTPUT".

 Template: MSG.BASE_PATH=<path>
 Example.: MSG.BASE_PATH=BBS:Conf.Requests/Msgbase/
 Usage...: Messagebase path for conference to post messages in, note that the
           string MUST end with a "/" or an ":".

 Template: MSG.MID_STRING=<string>
 Example.: MSG.MID_STRING=esc[34m|esc[0m
 Usage...: Separation string for bulletin created via "BULL.OUTPUT".
 BTW.....: Use Leftamiga+Ctrl+Esc to get an escape character in a tooltype
           editor.

 Template: MSG.PATTERN=<path:filename>
 Example.: MSG.PATTERN=Doors:Request/Message.dsg
 Usage...: Location of the design for the message output. @{"Creating Design" LINK MESSAGE}

 Template: MSG.SUBJECT=<string>
 Example.: MSG.SUBJECT=MOST WANTED!!
 Usage...: Simply the subject for the letters that will be created.

 Template: MSG.POST_TO=<string>
 Example.: MSG.POST_TO=EALL
 Usage...: User to post the messages to, "EALL" or "ALL" is recommended.

 Template: ACS.DELETE_ALL=<access>
 Example.: ACS.DELETE_ALL=255
 Usage...: Minimum of access to delete any request (not just your own!!).

 Template: DATAFILE_PATH=<path:filename>
 Example : DATAFILE_PATH=Doors:Request/Request.data
 Usage...: Path to use when creating a datafile. Note that you CAN'T use this
           new data with v1.0.


@{"[ Back to main ]" LINK MAIN}
@endnode

@node MESSAGE "Message Creation"

                             @{bg fill}@{fg highlight} MESSAGE CREATION @{fg text}@{bg background}

 These can be used anywhere in the text pattern:

 %DT - Current Date
 %UN - Username/Handle
 %LT - Location/Group
 %RQ - File Requested
 %CM - Longer Description

 If the user choose NOT to enter a longer comment the rows that starts with
 an "°" character will be skipped. And if the user choose to enter a longer
 comment these row's will be shown, but ofcourse does the "°" char not show!

 --- cut --- cut --- cut --- cut --- cut --- cut --- cut --- cut ---

    Current Date: %DT
 Username/Handle: %UN
  Location/Group: %LT

  Requested file: %RQ

 ° Longer description..
 ° : %CM
 °
 --- cut --- cut --- cut --- cut --- cut --- cut --- cut --- cut ---

@{"[ Back to main ]" LINK MAIN}
@endnode

